# 
# https://w3id.org/spot/am#hasNormalizedCoordinateValue
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#hasNormalizedCoordinateValue> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#hasNormalizedCoordinateValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/spot/am#BoundaryPoint> .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#hasNormalizedCoordinateValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Literal> .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#hasNormalizedCoordinateValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Specifies the position of a boundary point in relation to the reference space as a\r\n        normalized coordinate value (typically between 0 and 1). If the boundary point mapping is additionally\r\n        related by a RELOC property, the normalized value is interpreted in reference to the area described by\r\n        the RELOC property.\r\n        E.g.: Point(Mapping) <reloc:containedInRight> RefSpace. +\r\n        Point(Mapping) <spot-am:hasNormalizedCoordinateValue> '0.5'.\r\n         --> Point '0.5' describes the center of the right area of the Reference Space"@en .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#hasNormalizedCoordinateValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has normalized coordinate value"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/spot/am#hasSourceToTargetAngle
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#hasSourceToTargetAngle> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#hasSourceToTargetAngle> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/spot/am#AxisMapping> .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#hasSourceToTargetAngle> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Literal> .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#hasSourceToTargetAngle> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Specifies the angle (in degrees) between the source and target axis"@en .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#hasSourceToTargetAngle> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has source to target angle"@en .
# 
# 
# 
# #################################################################
# #
# #    Classes
# #
# #################################################################
# 
# 
# https://w3id.org/spot/am#Accuracy
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#Accuracy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#Accuracy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The level of accuracy for an axis mapping. Can be derived from angles if provided."@en .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#Accuracy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Accuracy"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/spot/am#AxisMapping
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#AxisMapping> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#AxisMapping> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The Axis Mapping is related to an Appearance of an Entity Space\r\n    and defines which Axis of the Entity Space (Source Axis) can be mapped to which Axis of the Reference Space\r\n     (another Entity, Document or Asset Space). This relation can be further specified with an angle and accuracy.\r\n     An AxisMapping object can only relate on Source Axis to one Reference Axis.\r\n     Thus, typically, each Entity Space Appearance links to three Axis Mapping objects."@en .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#AxisMapping> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Axis Mapping"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/spot/am#BoundaryPoint
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#BoundaryPoint> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#BoundaryPoint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A point that defines a boundary of an Entity Space on a specific Axis. "@en .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#BoundaryPoint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Boundary Point"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/spot/am#BoundaryPointMapping
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#BoundaryPointMapping> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#BoundaryPointMapping> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The Boundary Point Mapping describes the relation of an Entity Axis Boundary Point (Source Point)\r\n        to the reference space. The relation can be expressed by Directional Properties of the RELOC Ontology\r\n        (e.g., containedInFront/Right/Bottom etc.) and/or as a Normalized Coordinate in relation to the reference space.\r\n        If both properties are given the the normalized coordinate is to be interpreted in the context of the area\r\n        defined by the RELOC Property (e.g., Point <reloc:containedInRight> RefSpace.\r\n        --> '0.5' describes the center of the Right Area of the Reference Space)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#BoundaryPointMapping> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Boundary Point Mapping"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/spot/am#MaxBoundaryPoint
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#MaxBoundaryPoint> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#MaxBoundaryPoint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/spot/am#BoundaryPoint> .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#MaxBoundaryPoint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A point that represents the maximum/upper boundary of an Entity Space on a specific Axis"@en .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#MaxBoundaryPoint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Maximum Boundary Point"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/spot/am#MinBoundaryPoint
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#MinBoundaryPoint> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#MinBoundaryPoint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/spot/am#BoundaryPoint> .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#MinBoundaryPoint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A point that represents the minimum/lower boundary of an Entity Space on a specific Axis "@en .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#MinBoundaryPoint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Minimum Boundary Point"@en .
